Here I'll add the `validMissileTarget` helper and use it in `fireMissile` with the energy refund. The target validity check in fireMissile is as follows:

```ts
let target: SimEntity | undefined;
if (targetId && targetId !== entity.id) {
  const t = this.entities.get(targetId);
  if (t && (t.kind === 'ship' || t.kind === 'ai-ship') && !t.destroyed &&
    vecLength(vecSub(t.ship.pos, nose)) <= weapon.range &&
    this.losClear(entity, t.ship.pos)) {
    target = t;
  }
}
```

However, this depends on `nose`. I'll write a helper that computes the nose internally:

```ts
/**
 * The missile's firing target as of the current moment (alive, in range from the nose, LOS) —
 * undefined if the firing cannot be resolved (silently discarded / refunded).
 */
private validMissileTarget(entity: SimEntity, targetId: string | undefined): SimEntity | undefined {
  if (!targetId || targetId === entity.id) return undefined;
  const t = this.entities.get(targetId);
  if (!t || (t.kind !== 'ship' && t.kind !== 'ai-ship') || t.destroyed) return undefined;
  const nose = vecAdd(entity.ship.pos, vecScale(quatRotateVector(entity.ship.quat, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 1 }), NOSE_OFFSET_M));
  if (vecLength(vecSub(t.ship.pos, nose)) > (WEAPON_BY_ID.missile.range ?? 800)) return undefined;
  if (!this.losClear(entity, t.ship.pos)) return undefined;
  return t;
}
```

Next, in fireMissile, replace the inline check with `const target = this.validMissileTarget(entity, targetId)`, and on denial refund the energy:

```ts
if (!target) {
  // The target was lost between acceptance and tick (or the ship was
  // swapped): refund the already-committed cost — a denied firing
  // consumes no energy.
  entity.energy = Math.min(ENERGY_MAX, (entity.energy ?? ENERGY_MAX) + (WEAPON_BY_ID.missile.energy ?? 0));
  this.log.debug(...);
  return;
}
```

Note that the missile's weapon parameter is WEAPON_BY_ID.missile anyway. No problem.

